WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.834
-Right now, though,
if you guys don't mind,

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:04.434
do you mind if I write out
some thank-you notes right now?

00:00:04.434 --> 00:00:05.534
Is that cool with you?

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:08.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:10.067
James -- James, can I get some
thank you note

00:00:10.067 --> 00:00:11.467
writing music, please?

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:12.667
♪♪

00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:15.167
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:18.400
-Oh, he's -- he's psyched.
-Yeah.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:20.234
-Guess he's got a couple
Red Bulls before the show.

00:00:20.234 --> 00:00:22.334
-Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.334 --> 00:00:24.200
Eee!

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:25.567
♪♪

00:00:25.567 --> 00:00:28.934
-Thank you, new speaker
of the House Mike Johnson,

00:00:28.934 --> 00:00:31.033
for being the first person
to win an election

00:00:31.033 --> 00:00:32.534
with the slogan,
"You've seen the best.

00:00:32.534 --> 00:00:33.901
Now vote for the rest."

00:00:33.901 --> 00:00:37.534
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]
Come on.

00:00:37.534 --> 00:00:41.300
Why not?
-Why not, man?

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:42.868
♪♪

00:00:42.868 --> 00:00:44.767
-Thank you, Reese's Pieces,

00:00:44.767 --> 00:00:46.367
for making me see
which one of my friends

00:00:46.367 --> 00:00:47.934
can't pronounce Reese's.

00:00:47.934 --> 00:00:49.067
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:00:49.067 --> 00:00:51.234
Oh, "Reesie's."

00:00:51.234 --> 00:00:53.234
-Reese's.
-"Reesie's" Piece --

00:00:53.234 --> 00:00:55.834
"Reesie's Piecies."
-"Reese's Piecies."

00:00:55.834 --> 00:00:57.234
-Reese's Pieces.

00:00:57.234 --> 00:00:59.100
-Reesie's Piecies feces.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.601 --> 00:01:01.901
♪♪

00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:04.501
-Thank you,
walking through a spider web,

00:01:04.501 --> 00:01:06.567
for turning me
into a black belt in karate.

00:01:06.567 --> 00:01:11.133
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:11.133 --> 00:01:13.534
-Whoa!

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.367
♪♪

00:01:18.367 --> 00:01:21.334
-Thank you, TikTok's
planned music festival,

00:01:21.334 --> 00:01:23.467
for promising to be
a fun gathering of people

00:01:23.467 --> 00:01:25.334
staring at their phones
for five hours.

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:28.400
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:01:34.467 --> 00:01:35.868
♪♪

00:01:35.868 --> 00:01:39.067
Thank you, Frankenstein,
for looking like the Hulk

00:01:39.067 --> 00:01:41.434
after dealing with Spectrum
customer service.

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:45.400
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:47.167
-Wow.
-What?

00:01:47.167 --> 00:01:49.133
-Spectrum?

00:01:49.133 --> 00:01:50.567
Are you gonna send that
to Frankenstein?

00:01:50.567 --> 00:01:51.868
-I have no idea.

00:01:51.868 --> 00:01:53.133
-So you're thanking
Frankenstein with that?

00:01:53.133 --> 00:01:54.400
-I don't know
who I'm thanking again.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:56.334
Am I thanking the Hulk?
-Thanking Frankenstein.

00:01:56.334 --> 00:01:57.667
-Oh, wait.
I'm thanking Frankenstein.

00:01:57.667 --> 00:01:59.300
-Yeah, Frankenstein.
-He looks like --

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:01.167
Because he looks like the Hulk

00:02:01.167 --> 00:02:03.234
after dealing with
Spectrum customer --

00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:04.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.934 --> 00:02:06.033
I don't know, man.

00:02:06.033 --> 00:02:07.100
-You got to put it
in the mail, right?

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.267
-Hey, man, you got to do it.

00:02:09.267 --> 00:02:10.968
-Yeah. Come on, Frank.
-Come on, man.

00:02:10.968 --> 00:02:13.200
Come on, Frank.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.234
-Frankie.

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:17.133
-Frankie boy.
-Come on, boy!

00:02:17.133 --> 00:02:19.067
You been dealing
with Spectrum customer service!

00:02:19.067 --> 00:02:21.000
-Whoo-ooh!

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:24.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.868 --> 00:02:26.000
-Are you going to send
that one?

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.701
-What's that?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.701 --> 00:02:29.033
-That other one,
you're gonna send it in?

00:02:29.033 --> 00:02:30.734
-The other one?
Uh, yeah, maybe.

00:02:30.734 --> 00:02:31.934
I might send it in,
I might not.

00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:33.267
I don't even know at this point.
-Just checking.

00:02:33.267 --> 00:02:34.634
-I don't know.
Thanks for checking, though.

00:02:34.634 --> 00:02:35.734
-Well, I want to make sure
you're okay.

00:02:35.734 --> 00:02:37.133
-Yeah, I will.

00:02:37.133 --> 00:02:40.033
-[ Breathes deeply ]

00:02:40.033 --> 00:02:41.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:42.734
♪♪

00:02:42.734 --> 00:02:46.000
-Thank you, "It's the
Great Pumpkin, Charlie Brown,"

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.567
for the scariest moment
in any "Peanuts" special,

00:02:48.567 --> 00:02:51.300
when you realize Sally is
just Charlie Brown in a wig.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:54.067
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:02:54.067 --> 00:02:55.734
♪♪

00:02:55.734 --> 00:02:58.467
-What?

00:02:58.467 --> 00:03:00.634
[ Applause ]

00:03:00.634 --> 00:03:02.000
-[ Imitating "Peanuts" teacher
speaking ]

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:05.968
-Probably Linus and Lucy.
-Yeah.

00:03:05.968 --> 00:03:07.300
♪♪

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:10.067
Thank you,
fun-size candy,

00:03:10.067 --> 00:03:12.667
for being the short kings
of the chocolate world.

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:14.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:14.167 --> 00:03:15.734
[ Both laugh ]

00:03:15.734 --> 00:03:18.734
-Wow!
Big fans of short kings.

00:03:18.734 --> 00:03:21.100
[ Laughing ]

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.701
♪♪

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:25.934
-Thank you, candy corn,
for being the most delicious way

00:03:25.934 --> 00:03:27.667
to eat a candle.
There you have it, everybody.

00:03:27.667 --> 00:03:29.167
Those are my thank-you notes.

